NAME
       ssh - secure shell client

SYNOPSIS
       ssh [-p port] user@host [command]

DESCRIPTION
       Opens an SSH-2 session. With a COMMAND it is run remotely and
       the connection closes; without one an interactive shell starts.

       Authentication is by public key when ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 exists
       and the server accepts it, otherwise by password. The ciphers
       offered are chacha20-poly1305 and AES-GCM.

OPTIONS
       -p N   connect to port N instead of 22

FILES
       ~/.ssh/id_ed25519       private key
       ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub   public key

EXAMPLES
       ssh user@10.0.0.1
       ssh -p 2222 user@host uptime

SEE ALSO
       sshd(1), ssh-keygen(1), scp via 9p(1)
